WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.538 --> 00:00:01.413
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:03.597
- When my tics come on, I don't

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:05.577
really have a defense against it.

00:00:05.577 --> 00:00:06.604
(clears throat)

00:00:06.604 --> 00:00:08.498
And sometimes it just sort of comes out

00:00:08.498 --> 00:00:11.581
in these explosive, spontaneous ways.

00:00:17.363 --> 00:00:19.239
I'm an actor with Tourette's.

00:00:19.239 --> 00:00:22.011
For a long time, I did
worry about exposing that

00:00:22.011 --> 00:00:23.208
'cause I thought it would affect

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.674
getting hired, and auditions,
whatever it might be.

00:00:25.674 --> 00:00:28.029
Now, I just put it on the table.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:28.895
(clears throat).

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.108
It feels great to own it.

00:00:31.108 --> 00:00:31.941
Huh.

00:00:33.988 --> 00:00:36.678
My show is about having
Tourette's Syndrome

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:39.261
and finding my own way with it.

00:00:40.468 --> 00:00:43.150
Tourette's Syndrome is
a neurological disorder

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.267
that you're born with.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.599
The stereotype about Tourette's

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:48.946
is that people will curse
uncontrollably, which people do.

00:00:48.946 --> 00:00:50.018
I've never done that.

00:00:50.018 --> 00:00:52.552
When I tic, I clear my
throat (clears throat),

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.172
I cough (clears throat), sometimes

00:00:54.172 --> 00:00:56.350
I make noises in my throat.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.183
Huh.

00:00:57.183 --> 00:01:00.350
So (clearing throat).

00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:03.784
You're welcome to use that if you want.

00:01:03.784 --> 00:01:06.186
(dramatic music)

00:01:06.186 --> 00:01:08.473
Yeah, riding the subway is rough.

00:01:08.473 --> 00:01:09.769
I still get nervous about it,

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.070
especially since I have this

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.523
throat-clearing, sniffing tic.

00:01:13.523 --> 00:01:14.769
(clears throat)

00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:15.829
I have Tourette's Syndrome.

00:01:15.829 --> 00:01:16.934
That's why I'm makin' that noise.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:17.767
I can't help it.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.693
When I'm acting, I don't tic.

00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:20.576
I remember.

00:01:20.576 --> 00:01:25.552
Somehow, I'm like, in this zone,
and I'm able to just focus.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.406
It kind of just, like, goes away,

00:01:27.406 --> 00:01:31.061
and it says, okay, take a
break, do what you love,

00:01:31.061 --> 00:01:33.058
and I'll be waitin' for
ya when ya come back.

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.808
(dramatic music)

